{
  "indoor": false,
  "camera_size": 24,
  "note": "白石街 (native:lancheng/white_gate … street_top; 第十章 B): the town where the wind stops — a white island under a pale sky with the cloud sea below its lip; round-shouldered houses of warm white plaster, slate roofs pale as the cloud, bronze bells under every eave and strings of small bells across the street; worn white slabs in rows, a groove trodden down the middle; moss on the lee of every wall, verdigris streaks under the bells; the 铃匠's open yard with the anvil and a bell half cast, the 萧家 yard shut and swept, its hook bright; the 风铃阁's three-eaved front at the top. No chimney anywhere: 不食人间烟火.",
